---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="NRR Acceleration Playbook — North End Technology"
  description="Systematically raise net revenue retention across the install base."
>
  <section class="playbook-hero section-alt">
    <div class="wrapper">
      <p class="eyebrow">Playbook</p>
      <h1>NRR Acceleration</h1>
      <p>
        Net revenue retention is the single metric a PE sponsor trusts more than any
        other. This playbook treats it as an engineering and product output, not a
        sales target.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrapper playbook-body">
      <h2>NRR is a platform problem before it's a sales problem</h2>
      <p>
        Expansion and retention both depend on how easily the platform can surface a
        customer's next unit of value. Fragmented product silos make that hard by
        design — each silo optimizes its own upsell path instead of the account's
        total footprint.
      </p>

      <h2>The acceleration sequence</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Instrument account-level usage, not product-level usage.</strong> NRR is an account metric; product-level dashboards routinely hide churn risk that only shows up at the account roll-up.</li>
        <li><strong>Build one expansion surface, not five.</strong> Consolidate cross-sell and upsell triggers onto shared platform infrastructure so every product team is expanding the same account model.</li>
        <li><strong>Close the loop between support and expansion.</strong> Escalating support tickets are a leading indicator of churn; route that signal into the same system that drives expansion motion.</li>
        <li><strong>Report NRR by cohort, not in aggregate.</strong> Aggregate NRR can mask a declining cohort behind a strong one — sponsors want to see the trend by vintage.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The platform payoff</h2>
      <p>
        Once expansion and retention run on shared account infrastructure, NRR
        improvement becomes a compounding platform effect rather than a one-time
        sales push — exactly the kind of durable metric movement a PE sponsor
        rewards at exit.
      </p>

      <div class="playbook-cta">
        <a href={`${base}/#contact`} class="btn btn-primary">Discuss this playbook</a>
        <a href={`${base}/#playbooks`} class="back-link">&larr; Back to all playbooks</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
